[1.332,"o","\u001b[H\r\u001b[6B\u001b[48;5;237m\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[38;5;231mPlease implement this issue.\u001b[39m                                                            \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231m#72 Catch vague invoice lines before they go out\u001b[39m                                        \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mCustomers' accounts payable keep sending invoices back because a line doesn't say what \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mit was for (\"Services\", \"Misc work\", \"Travel\"): nine last quarter, each one paid weeks \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mlate. Add \u001b[38;5;153minvoicer review <file>\u001b[38;5;231m: it asks the model whether each line of each invoice \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231msays clearly enough what we delivered, prints the lines that don't, with why, and exits\u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mwith 1 when it finds one. Then run it in CI on the files in \u001b[38;5;153minvoices/\u001b[38;5;231m, so that a pull \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mrequest with a vague line can't be merged.\u001b[39m                                              \r\u001b[1B                                                                                          \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mMaria in accounting is the one who sends them back to us. She went through last \u001b[39m        \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mquarter's invoices and graded lines clear or vague, each with her reason: \u001b[39m              \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;153mevals/line-clarity.jsonl\u001b[38;5;231m. The check has to agree with her: catch at least 9 in 10 of \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mthe lines she'd call vague, and pass at least 9 in 10 of the ones she'd call clear. We \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;5;231mdon't want it blocking good invoices.\u001b[39m                                                   \r\u001b[7B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;5;174m*\u001b[3GP\u001b[38;5;216muzz\u001b[38;5;174mling… \r\u001b[3B\u001b[38;5;246m❯ \u001b[39m\u001b[7m \u001b[27m\u001b[K\u001b[34;1H\u001b[32;3H"]
